  "2026-11-01T16:44:44.523Z",codex-agent,"Diagnosis reproduced on CI Node 26.13.0: V8 uses signed 32-bit block counters. Calling the existing depth scanner on a valid 16 MiB JSON string 130 times overflows its per-character loop counter to -2113929216. Native TestCoverage maps that negative count to tracker-record.ts lines 20-25 (six lines). It counts covered lines with count > 0, while the spec reporter lists only count == 0; negative counts therefore lower 77/83 lines to 92.77% without an uncovered-lines listing. This is not duplicate-module attribution. Raw profile and native summary agree. The focused reproduction has unrelated uncalled functions, so it is diagnosis rather than a full-gate claim. Fix direction: scan JSON punctuation in native RegExp rather than running a JS branch for every ordinary string character; preserve bounds and escaping semantics and add a raw-counter regression. This should also remove the dominant repeated-validation CPU cost from the exhaustive properties."
  "2026-11-01T16:54:39.384Z",codex-agent,"The raw-counter regression fails with only depthSafe restored to the previous implementation (169.77 s, negative native V8 count) and passes after restoration of the punctuation scanner (about 1.6 s). Full JSON boundary tests pass 10/10, including 500 seeded byte/depth/escaping transports. Duration changes retain every existing boundary and corruption pair: independent transitions run with at most two cooperative workers; each corruption pair uses a clone of one prepared final native tracker, so its bad write cannot inflate every later case history. No sampling or case-count reduction is used. The exact npm run coverage command is now running with Node 26.13.0, Bun 1.3.14, isolated identity and unchanged source list/threshold flags. Local PATH deliberately omits Docker under the task rules; backend-only skips will be reported separately. README, decision-evidence docs and lease docstrings now state SDK acquisition confinement depends on pm-cli#1647 and link pm-rl-confined-sdk-locks."
  "2026-11-01T17:48:06.279Z",codex-agent,"The full exact-command run has completed the immutable snapshot sweep: all 337 snapshot checks and 1910 card corruption checks remain, with 3 generations/4 receipts/10 card variants and 21 historical replays. Duration is 309.609 s locally versus 3009.822 s in the failing CI log (different host, same Node 26.13.0). Pure concurrency without causal reduction remained too expensive in diagnostics. The final sequential reduction retains every live/history edge that its selected peer can affect and every observed write. Only reads outside the verified peer write set, the unchanged project prefix, and immutable births already present in the prepared inventory can commute. Each executed peer is checked against all native data/history outside its mask and all prepared birth records; any wider write invalidates the proof. Native/held-lease generation changes end each region. Fixed seed 0x1071647 chooses one native witness per commuting region, with first/last of every observation kind retained. No snapshot-corruption pairs are sampled. The proof is documented in test/fixtures/README-sweep-equivalence.md. Earlier comments describing an all-raw-edge attempt are intermediate, not the final sampling claim."
  "2026-11-01T18:09:59.267Z",codex-agent,"Implementation checkpoint: depthSafe now skips ordinary JSON text using native punctuation search; the max-size valid JSON stress test fails on the reverted scanner with negative V8 counts and passes after restoration. The old six loop-body lines 20-25 receive count -2113929216 after 130 encodings of 16777216 bytes; native Node coverage counts only positive lines while displaying only zero-count uncovered lines, explaining 77/83 = 92.77% with an empty uncovered column. This is signed counter overflow, not duplicate module loading. No coverage configuration, threshold or ignore changes. Current prepared-clone corruption sweep retains 337 snapshot checks and 1910 card checks, measured at 309.609 s versus 3009.822 s in failing CI. Sequential sweep proof additionally checks the actual native observation before/after each sampled peer, protects unrelated tracker bytes and every creation event, and refuses any completion-order reclassification of a mutable edge. Full exact npm run coverage and final sequential timings remain pending at this checkpoint. README and decision-evidence documentation explicitly defer SDK lock acquisition confinement to pm-cli#1647 and link pm-rl-confined-sdk-locks."
  "2026-11-01T18:11:10.046Z",codex-agent,"Focused timing checkpoint: reject/sdk-reject passes on Node 26.13.0 with native V8 coverage: 942 discovered edges, 121 exercised interleavings and 47 deep-equal native commutation witnesses, 333.685 s test duration (334.953 s process). The failing CI sweep executed all 942 edges per peer and measured roughly 1470-1630 s per reject transition; these are different hosts, so the final CI duration target remains to be verified. The first empirical proof attempt exposed an observation-bookkeeping bug under parallel native birth reads; retaining the exact observation across awaits fixes it. Actual pre-injection classification now also rejects any reordered mutable edge assigned a commuting baseline slot. No package runtime race assertion was weakened. Check/typecheck/lint/duplicates and build:test pass; duplicates reports zero clones; docstring reports 58 files and 523 declarations; changelog generation/check and append-only history prefix verification pass. Full coverage remains in progress."
  "2026-11-01T18:18:52.059Z",codex-agent,"Final packed receipt for runtime source eb45517411f488385ebb4112254a106706fecdcd: six fresh acceptance executions pass (Node/Bun x evaluation-compatibility, decision-evidence, sequential-evaluation), plus two retained-fixture resume replays and two native fixture preparations. Archive SHA-256 69f9b9568ec3b5d0ea4e06b24be56e3a905ae72c1bbb98a142ecad989361c820; 241 shipped files, including 180 runtime files, independently compared byte-for-byte with the working-tree pack and the certified archive. Public source 26650e303ec2cb6fcdc6c51092bcc30b2f1ed27c remains read-only and digest-unchanged: 113 items, 92 done-role items. All three generated documents describe this cohort; retained report, evidence root, same-command envelope sizes and source digest replay successfully. Search for 120e20e in docs and README is empty. Initial private pack setup lacked gzip; adding that utility to the private no-Docker tool path fixed setup before any acceptance was executed. No runtime or receipt check was weakened. The selector test also passes through pm test (1/1); its linked focused suite skip pattern now names the new sweep accurately. The full coverage run continues; one packed LM wall-clock assertion exceeded 20 s under contention and will be rerun alone unchanged."
  "2026-11-01T19:01:53.146Z",codex-agent,"Progress: the exact one-worker CI coverage command is still running on Node 26.13.0, with 28 of the 30 exhaustive-path/peer sweeps completed so far and every native commutation/foreign-byte assertion passing. The private outer launcher allowance was extended; repository test clocks, coverage thresholds and source scope are unchanged. The remaining sequential work retains all affected edges (reject peers discovered 942 each; SDK rejection exercised 121, package rejection 133, sealing 62 and stopping 72). To bring whole-job duration toward the requested 1.5x-main target, the next bounded change will use two independent native test-file workers after this exact-flags diagnostic run finishes. A real two-file rendezvous regression will prove concurrency and merged 100% source coverage, including a function-only revert proof; no coverage attribution arithmetic or thresholds will change."
  "2026-11-01T19:24:14.264Z",codex-agent,"Exact CI-flags diagnostic complete: npm run coverage on Node 26.13.0 / Bun 1.3.14, one native file worker, 1461 tests: 1441 pass, one LM timing assertion fails, 19 Docker cases skip because local Docker access is prohibited. tracker-record.ts is now 86/86 lines and 84/84 raw V8 blocks, all branches/functions covered; 287 root-source profiles have zero negative counters and at most one canonical root-source instance per profile. The LM case took 21851 ms against 20000 ms; the unchanged isolated rerun passes at 13161 ms, so this is host contention. Global local coverage retains Docker-only external-LM gaps (index.ts 4505-4506, process-lm.ts 60-64); no threshold or source exemption was changed. The raw block calculator additionally found non-Docker gaps hidden behind the former native line failure: sparse Run optional fields; prospective wrong identity; reordered retained graph fallback; completed-receipt native read failure and legacy unversioned snapshot label; and an unreachable meta throw. Four new real-SDK tests cover the reachable cases with code/exit assertions. meta.ts now removes the unreachable arm: refuse.ts:18-23 asserts PmCliExpectedError on return and throws every other value, so the following unconditional meta_reservation_drift refusal is exhaustive. Existing transient-approval behavior still passes. Focused linked run: 6/6. No SDK responses were mocked."
  "2026-11-01T19:24:15.166Z",codex-agent,"Duration evidence: sequential snapshot sweep was 11030.827 s in failing CI and is 1972.589 s locally with the same five paths and six peers; every affected edge remains, with 1229 native interleavings representing 8112 discovered edge/peer positions. Fixed seed 0x1071647, first/last by kind, creation-event protection, unrelated-byte hashes and actual SDK before/after observations certify only commuting regions. Corruption sweep was 3009.822 s in CI and is 309.609 s locally, retaining all 337 snapshot checks and 1910 card checks. Hosts differ; final job duration remains a CI claim. Native test-file concurrency now uses the permitted bound of two to parallelize independent suites, without changing the source list, ignore list, attribution arithmetic or thresholds. Behavioral revert proof: reverting only runGate to one worker makes the two-file real native rendezvous fail after 10.579 s; restoring it passes, including 100% aggregate coverage for two separately exercised source functions. The final full two-worker command will run before the single push."
  "2026-11-01T20:16:34.561Z",codex-agent,"Two-worker final coverage run remains in progress without a reported test failure. The bounded real concurrency regression, all four new block cases, max-size JSON counter stress, and packed LM timing acceptance have passed within this full run. The corruption sweep retains 337/1910 checks at 315.643 s in the two-worker run. All 512 seeded card cases and the complete EIO/ENOSPC/SIGKILL card transaction matrix pass. Native commutation witnesses now compare deep copies on both sides, preventing SDK object aliasing from mutating the saved observation; this test-harness strengthening was applied before the sequential module loads. No runtime source changed after cf0e21f. The existing packed receipt for eb45517 will be superseded by a fresh final-runtime acceptance cohort after the full run completes."
  "2026-11-01T20:32:08.074Z",codex-agent,"Superseding packed receipt for final runtime cf0e21f730b06fdb5b8b7bc88ad848fded02dbae: archive SHA-256 4ea2845631f959481923b9d6a9fa591fdfe2dfc41191dcdbd3758bd352de5e82. Six fresh Node/Bun acceptance runs pass, plus two retained-fixture replays and two fixture preparations. Independent working-tree pack matches every byte of all 241 shipped files (180 runtime files). Public source remains 26650e303ec2cb6fcdc6c51092bcc30b2f1ed27c, 113 items and 92 done-role items, read-only with unchanged source digest. All three generated evidence documents describe this final cohort; recorded resume report, root and same-command byte counts replay exactly. The evidence-consistency linked test passes again. This supersedes the eb45517 archive receipt, which remains historical evidence in earlier comments. Only one native coverage worker remained before starting acceptance, so active test execution stayed within two workers."
  "2026-11-01T21:01:19.822Z",codex-agent,"Final two-worker npm run coverage result on Node 26.13.0: 1466 tests, 1447 passed, zero failed, 19 prohibited-Docker cases skipped; native duration 5447.220 s, process 5460.313 s. tracker-record.ts is 86/86 lines and 84/84 measured V8 blocks, 100% branches/functions; all 287 canonical root-source profiles have no negative counters and no duplicate root-source instance within a profile. Raw non-Docker block gaps are closed: evaluation-plan.ts and meta.ts now fully cover their measured blocks. Strict global gate exits 1 solely for Docker-only index.ts 4505-4506 and process-lm.ts 60-64: 22458/22465 lines, 9004/9006 branches, 1792/1795 functions, 8636/8645 blocks. No exemption or threshold reduction was applied. These external-LM paths remain covered by the existing real Docker CI tests; local Docker access is forbidden. The LM timing case passes in this full run. Final sweep passes all 30 path/peer combinations, 1229 certified interleavings over 8112 discovered positions; duration 2164.405 s versus 11030.827 s in failing CI. Corruption remains 337 snapshot/1910 card checks, 315.643 s versus 3009.822 s in failing CI. Whole local native run fell from 8086.585 s with one file worker to 5447.220 s with two despite five added tests. Host contention varies; the 1.5x-main CI duration target is pending the pushed-head run. Check (typecheck/lint/duplicates=0), build:test, docstring (58 files/523 declarations), diff/privacy and regenerated-evidence consistency checks pass. Final CI handoff is pending at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/107/checks; actual new run/job URLs will be reported after the single push without waiting."
